// A string store that appends to its own target in place. `s = s + x` builds
// its result in the block `s` holds (the consuming concat of the runtime), so
// the old value is neither copied nor freed. One cell says which variable node
// may be consumed: it is set while the right-hand side of such a store is
// emitted and holds -1 the rest of the time (esc_init makes it, so it exists
// whether or not the analysis is on, and no store finds anything else there).

esc_cons_set(int leaf) {
  int ecs_old = (import esc_cons)[0];
  integer_list_set((import esc_cons), 0, leaf);
} return int ecs_old;
